Subject: Re: How can I get the source code of JGR
Message-ID: <1329AAEF-D3AE-4F05-9252-1B56AEF26C43@r-project.org>

> Hi, Guys
>
> I want to know how I can get the source code of JGR. It seems that  
> the so-called source code package of JGR on the website only  
> contains the source code of the launcher.

Since R cannot necessarily compile Java code R source packages cannot  
include Java sources, they have to be pre-compiled. The Java source  
code is, however, available from the SVN.


>  Java classes within the JGR.jar is already compiled and I cannot  
> check the contents. I just wonder if JGR is open source and if so,  
> how can I get the source. Thanks
>

Yes and yes (svn://svn.rforge.net/org/trunk/rosuda/JGR).

Cheers,
Simon

